{"name":"Court-Bouillon","hex":"#cecb97","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"court","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An enclosed space; a courtyard; an uncovered area shut in by the walls of a building, or by different buildings; also, a space opening from a street and nearly surrounded by houses; a blind alley.","A street with no outlet, a cul-de-sac."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To seek to achieve or win (a prize).","To risk (a consequence, usually negative)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/court"},{"term":"bouillon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clear seasoned broth made by simmering usually light meat, such as beef or chicken.\nA similar broth made by reconstituting, that is, by adding hot water to dried powder concentrate; the dried powder concentrate itself.","A similar broth made by reconstituting, that is, by adding hot water to dried powder concentrate; the dried powder concentrate itself."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bouillon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Court-bouillon","blocks":[{"text":"Court-bouillon or court bouillon is a quickly-cooked broth used for poaching other foods, most commonly fish or seafood. It is also sometimes used for poaching vegetables, eggs, sweetbreads, cockscombs, and delicate meats. It includes seasonings and salt but lacks animal gelatin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Poached_halibut_in_a_sesame_court_bouillon.jpg/330px-Poached_halibut_in_a_sesame_court_bouillon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Court-bouillon","wikidata":"Q3001487"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"court":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/En-uk-caught.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transc